<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    What Android's Auto Backup may carry to a reinstall or a new phone. Devices below API 31 read
    this file; API 31+ read `data_extraction_rules.xml`, which excludes the same paths.

    Everything Omni owns lives in Firestore under the signed-in account, so a restore has nothing
    to bring back that signing in would not bring back anyway. The one directory that must *not*
    travel is DataStore's:

      * `onboarding_seen` — a restored `true` is why an install can open straight onto sign-in with
        no introduction. A first launch on a phone is a first launch, whatever the cloud remembers.
      * the step counter's anchor and boot id — device-specific by construction (`StepState`). Another
        phone's anchor is a meaningless number here, and restoring it makes the day's step count wrong
        rather than merely absent.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="file" path="datastore" />
</full-backup-content>
